                       <seg type="rubrication">Divine names (name of God in <ref target="#ms_i1.1"/>(occasionally
                           only a few letters within the word); name of St Mary in <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/> and <ref target="ms_i1.5"/>);
                           titles and numbers of the Psalms and Canticles; incipits and numbers of
                           Songs; titles of <ref target="#ms_i1.2"/>, <ref target="#ms_i1.3"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/>; title and incipit of the daily
                           readings of  <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/>; name and traditional interpretation of the Hebrew
                           letters in Psalm 118; refrains of <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/> (written out fully or
                          abbreviated); letters <foreign xml:lang="gez">አ</foreign> and <foreign xml:lang="gez">ጽ</foreign> in the word <foreign xml:lang="gez">አምጽኡ</foreign> in Psalms 27 and 95; letter
                          <foreign xml:lang="gez">ቃ</foreign> in the word <foreign xml:lang="gez">ቃለ</foreign> in Psalm 27; letters <foreign xml:lang="gez">የ</foreign> and <foreign xml:lang="gez">ነ</foreign> in the word 
                          <foreign xml:lang="gez">የማነ</foreign> in Psalm 117;
                          letters <foreign xml:lang="gez">ግ</foreign> and <foreign xml:lang="gez">ዩ</foreign> in the word <foreign xml:lang="gez">ግነዩ</foreign> in Psalm 135; letters <foreign xml:lang="gez">ስ</foreign> and <foreign xml:lang="gez">ሕ</foreign> in the word
                             <foreign xml:lang="gez">ስብሕዎ</foreign> in Psalm 150; letters <foreign xml:lang="gez">ባ</foreign> and <foreign xml:lang="gez">ክ</foreign> of the word <foreign xml:lang="gez">ይባርክዎ</foreign> in Canticle 10;
                           elements of the punctuation signs and text dividers; Ethiopic numerals or
                           their elements. A few groups of lines (alternating with black
                           lines) on the opening pages of <ref target="#ms_i1.1"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/>; two lines (alternating
                           with a black line) on the opening page of <ref target="#ms_i1.2"/></seg>
                     </handNote>
