                  <additions>
                     <list>
                        <item xml:id="a1">
                           <locus target="#3r"/>
                           <desc type="DonationNote">The note is written by the same hand as <ref target="#a3">Additio 3.</ref> It states that
                              the manuscript was donated to <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0171KY">St John the Baptist, Dabra Betel of Kokolo</placeName> by 
                              <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15215LegAdarago"><roleName type="title">Lǝğ</roleName>ʾAdarāğo.</persName></desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez">ዝመጽሐፍ፡ ዘልጅ፡ አደራጆ፡ ዘወኃቦ፡ ለቅዱስ፡ ዮሐንስ፡
                              ኮኮሎ፡ ደብረ፡ ቤቴል፡ ገበዙ፡ ቄሥ፡ በራኪ፡ የአለቃ፡ ተሥፋይ፡ ልጅ</q>
                               </item>
                        <item xml:id="a2">
                           <locus target="#3r"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText">Protective prayer. Below the note there are two drawings in <term key="MagicSymbols" ana="#MagicSymbols">angelic script</term>.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez">በስመ፡ አብ፡ በል፡ ዘይነግሥ፡ በረድኤተ፡ ልዑል፡ ጸሎተ፡
                              በረድ፡ ወፀብዕ፡ ወኵያናት፡ አረር፡ ጠቅልል፡ የሐፍር፡</q>
                          </item>
                        <item xml:id="a3">
                           <locus target="#3v"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText"><title type="incomplete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT4245Prayer">Prayer for the twilight</title>The note is hardly legible due to faded ink.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez">ወካዕበ፡ ናስተበቍዕ፡ ለዕፀ፡ ቅዱስ፡ መስቀል፡ ጽኑዓ፡ ሥልጣን፡</q>                             
                        </item>
                        <item xml:id="a4">
                           <locus target="#133vb"/>
                           <desc type="DonationNote"/>
                           <q xml:lang="gez"> <q xml:lang="am">ዝዳዊት፡ ዘልጅ፡ አደራጆ፡ ሥሙ፡ ገብረ፡ ኢየሱስ፡
                              የአባታቸው፡ ሥም፡ ገብረኪዳን፡ የናታቸው፡ ሥም፡ ወለተ፡ ሥላሴ፡ ወለተ፡ ተክለ፡ ሐ{ይ}ማኖት፡ እህታቸው፡
                              ወለተ፡ ሥላሴ፡ ገብ <gap reason="lost"/>የእህታቸው ልጅ፡ ወለተ፡ ኪዳን፡ ልጃቸው፡ ምሺታቸው፡ አመተ፡ ማርያም፡
                              ዘወሐቦ፡ ለቅዱስ፡ ዮሐንስ፡ ደብረ፡ ቤቴል፡ ኮኮሎ፡ ዘሠረቆ፡ ወዘፈሐቆ፡ በስልጣ [sic]፡ ጴጥሮስ፡ ወጳውሎስ፡
                              በስልጣነ፡ ፫፻ውጉዝ፡ ከመ፡ አርዮስ፡ ዘሰረቆ፡ ወዘፈሐቆ፡</q></q>
                           <note> The note is written in Gǝʿǝz and Amharic. It states that the Ms.
                              was donated to the church of St John the Baptist, Dabra Betel of
                              Kokolo by <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15215LegAdarago"><roleName type="title">Lǝğ</roleName>ʾAdarāğo</persName>, whose baptismal name is Gabra ʾIyasus. Also,
                              his close relatives are mentioned: his father <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15230GabraKidan">Gabra Kidān</persName>, 
                              his mother <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15236WalattaSelTakla">Walatta Śǝllāse Walatta Takla Hāymānot</persName>, 
                              his sister <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15234WalattaSellase">Walatta Śǝllāse</persName>,
                              his spouse <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15238AmataMaryam">ʾAmata Māryām</persName>,
                              his niece <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15237WalattaKid">Walatta Kidān</persName> and his nameless child.</note>
                        </item>
                        <item xml:id="a5">
                           <locus from="131ra" to="133va"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText"><title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2940RepCh221">The name of the scribe has been erased.</title></desc>
                           <quote xml:lang="gez"/>
                           </item>
                        <item xml:id="e1">
                           <locus target="#53r"/>
                           <desc>The midpoint of the ‘Psalms of David’ is marked. Six letters in the line are rubricated, in the <ref target="h1">main hand.</ref></desc>
                        </item>
                        <item xml:id="e2">
                           <locus target="#53r"/> 
                           <desc>To the right there is an inscription <foreign xml:lang="gez">ዝየ፡ መንፈቁ፡ ለዳዊት</foreign> added later, in a secondary hand.
                              </desc>
                           </item>
                        <item xml:id="e3">
                           <locus target="#7v #9r #10r #16r #17r #29r #47r #57v #82r #93v #101v #115r"/>
                           <desc>The scribe reduced the size of his handwriting to accommodate the whole line or the end of the line.</desc>
                        </item>
                        <item xml:id="e4">
                           <locus target="#5rv #8r #9v #19r #31r #44v #51r #62r #73v #90v"/>
                          <desc>Part of the line is taken up.</desc>
                           </item>
                        <item xml:id="e5">
                           <locus target="#22v"/>
                           <desc>Tamallas-signs, in the shape of a cross or/and a crude inscription <foreign xml:lang="gez">ተመለስ</foreign>, indicating the place where the omission, written in the
                           margins, belong. </desc>
                        </item>
                           <item xml:id="e6"> 
                              <locus target="#2v"/>
                              <desc>Traces of an erased text still visible.</desc>
                              </item>
                        <item xml:id="e7">
                           <locus target="#1r #2rv #3r #4r #51v #52v #55v #56r"/>
                           <desc>Scribbles, doodles.</desc>
                        </item>
                     </list>
                  </additions>
                  <bindingDesc>
                     <binding contemporary="partly">
                        <decoNote xml:id="b1">Two wooden boards.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b2" type="Cover">Dark brown <term key="tooling" ana="#tooling">tooled</term> leather.
                           (at least 4 tools were used: <term key="tripleStraightLine" ana="#tripleStraightLine">triple line fillet</term>, <term key="singleCircle" ana="#singleCircle">single circle</term>,  interlaced line fillet, cross hatching. 
                           <term key="textileInlay" ana="#textileInlay">Textile inlays.</term>
                        </decoNote>
                           <decoNote xml:id="b3" type="Sewing">Two pairs of sewing stations.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b4" type="SewingStations">4</decoNote>                        
                        <decoNote xml:id="b5" type="bindingMaterial">
                           <material key="wood"/>
                           <material key="leather"/>
                           <material key="textile"/>
                        </decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b6" type="Endbands">The endbands are present.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b7" type="Other">Two pairs of chains of endband stitches at the spine cover.</decoNote>
                          </binding>
                  </bindingDesc>
